    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "There are five different kinds of fruit in a bowl: apple, grapes, cherries, strawberry and banana.\n\n- Ali likes cherries.\n- Ben likes apple, grapes, cherries, strawberry and banana.\n- Cam likes cherries, strawberry and banana.\n- Dan likes cherries and banana.\n- Eli likes grapes and cherries.\n\nEach of them gets one piece of fruit that they like and each of them gets a different kind of fruit.\n\nWhich fruit does Ben get?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "apple"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "grapes"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "cherries"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "strawberry"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "banana"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Start with the child who likes only one fruit",
        "body": "Ali only likes cherries, so Ali gets the cherries. Then Dan must get the banana, Cam must get the strawberry (cherries and banana are taken), and Eli must get the grapes (cherries are taken). The only fruit left is the apple, so Ben gets the apple.\n\n**Answer: (A) apple**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Start with the fruit nobody else likes",
        "body": "Five children get five different fruits, so every fruit is given out, including the apple. Only Ben likes the apple, so Ben gets it.\n\n**Answer: (A) apple**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "logic"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
