    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The Maths Metro line has six stations, as shown on the map. The train stops at every station. When it reaches one of the two end stations, it changes direction. A train driver started driving at station 2 and his first stop was at station 3.\n\nWhich station was his 96th stop?",
    "image": "qimages/ukmt/pk-sample/q08.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find the repeating pattern",
        "body": "The stops are 3, 4, 5, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 2, and then the pattern repeats (the next stop is 3 again). So the pattern has 10 stops. $96=9\\times10+6$, so the 96th stop is the same as the 6th stop, which is station 4.\n\n**Answer: (D) 4**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count how far he has travelled",
        "body": "Between the end stations 1 and 6 the train travels 5 steps each way, so a full round trip is 10 steps. Starting at station 2 and moving east, after 10 steps he is back at station 2 moving east, so after 90 steps he is at station 2 again. Six more steps: 3, 4, 5, 6, 5, 4. So the 96th stop is station 4.\n\n**Answer: (D) 4**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "patterns",
      "logic"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": "The sample PDF has no answer key; answer solved independently."
  },
